  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syrian Coastal Areas Response 2025 - SIDA RRM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 6 -months project aims to provide an improved access to basic and protection assistance for affected population of the recent violence in the coastal areas in Syria. This is part of Oxfam&apos;s 18 -months response plan to the crisis erupted on March 6, 2025. The response plans provide integrated Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), protection, and Emergency Food Security and Vulnerable Livelihood (EFSVL) services to help save lives and restore peace to the affected areas. Under this project, Oxfam response will be focused on providing protection services to the most affected individuals. As it will provide individual protection, distribute dignity kits, kits for Pregnant and Lactating Women (PLW), and psychosocial support services. This project will provide services to a total of 4,458 individuals of the affected population, including Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs), returnees, and host communities. At least 80% of the beneficiaries are women and girls of which 1600 will benefit from dignity and PLW kits. Number of direct beneficiaries IDPs, Host Communities, Communities affected by the violence (Women, girls, men, and boys). This project will benefit 4,458 individuals, of which 80% are expected to be women and girls and 20% are men and boys. The demographic composition of the target communities includes 89% host communities, 9% IDPs and 2% returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
